# Jarvis-First Priority Rule

Current project priority is standalone Jarvis first.

- Do not prioritize new Discord features or live Discord verification.
- Keep existing Discord/Digital Me code compiling and preserve compatibility.
- Jarvis Core must be transport/client agnostic.
- Prefer standalone text/UI/voice test paths that require no Discord.
- Prioritize core, memory, tools, standalone UI, standalone voice, permissions, and runtime architecture.
- Defer Discord runtime persona/voice decoupling and DiscordJarvisAdapter migration until Jarvis Core v1 reaches its definition-of-done gate.
- Preserve all existing Discord consent/privacy rules even while Discord work is deferred.
- Do not delete existing Discord code as "unused".
